Hi Florian,

                The Forum thread https://openflexure.discourse.group/t/alte=
rnative-file-options-other-than-stl-for-block-delta-stages/1438 explains ou=
r CAD pipeline in answer to a similar question. This design process there a=
pplies to the Microscope as well as to the other stages.

                For your particular need, the OpenSCAD changes are minimal,=
 and from what you have said about your software development the code-based=
 CAD will probably make a lot of sense to you. The advice from https://open=
flexure.discourse.group/t/arducam-b0196-on-high-resolution-v7-microscope/23=
93/3 is similar, although the mount for the Pi HQ camera is not currently i=
n the main repository. You will need to clone the repository at the branch =
https://gitlab.com/openflexure/openflexure-microscope/-/tree/hq_camera. The=
n you should be able to set `CAMERA =3D "picamera_hq";` in the file `rms_op=
tics_module.scad` and then build it with OpenSCAD. It should give you an op=
tics module with the HQ camera mount. This still has the f=3D50mm lens. To =
change that you just need to find the configuration function `rms_f50d13_co=
nfig` in `optics_configurations.scad`. There are two things that you need t=
o change, the nominal focal length, "tube_lens_f", and the back focal dista=
nce of the lens that you are using "tube_lens_ffd" (this is a little shorte=
r than the focal length). That should build the optics module that you need=
.
                If you need help understanding the project and the CAD, ple=
ase post your questions on the Forum (https://openflexure.discourse.group/)=
 so that the solutions are available to all.

William

