Hey Julian!

Sorry for necrobumping, but I just want to give you a heads up on the proje=
ct, which you might find interesting.

For high resolution pictures, we started to implement the IMX477 camera, ma=
king us switch from a 50 mm focal length achromatic doublet to a 125 mm mm =
focal length achromatic doublet (both 12.7 mm in diameter).

My job will soon be to refactor the affected parts to use most of the resou=
rces of the given camera. Now, the team I am working with uses AutoCAD occa=
sionally but mostly Solid Edge for model manipulation. I am a rookie to thi=
s, but as far as my understanding is correct, scaling a part up is just don=
e by setting the according parameters - hard to build, but easy to replicat=
e.

I will go down the road to deliver the message, that if something is alread=
y perfectly built, nothing needs to change, but do you happen to know any r=
eliable way to provide those guys with some PAR files to play with?

I cannot be the only one, who this is happening to. Why must it be so hard,=
 when it can come so easy?

Alright, father Julian. Thank you for your attention. I hope this made your=
 day.

Thankfully

Florian
